# Optional daemon environment for a COLD start (no daemon running to read from).
#
# `bin/daemon_restart.sh` carries every AIIDA_PINO_*/PINO_* variable forward from the
# running daemon, so a normal restart needs nothing here. This file only matters when
# there is no daemon to read -- the first start after a reboot, or after a full stop.
#
# Copy to `daemon.env` (untracked) and fill in values for THIS machine. Keep hostnames
# and paths here, never in a tracked file.
#
#   cp daemon.env.example daemon.env
#
# Override the location with AIIDA_PINO_DAEMON_ENV=/path/to/file.

# Computer label whose staged collections may have stride/crop applied at READ time
# instead of being materialised. Unset disables the demotion, which makes every
# submission carrying a stride fail validate_inputs with exit 303.
# AIIDA_PINO_REMOTE_READ_TIME=<computer-label>

# Per-material overlay channels. Unset raises on any case that needs one.
# PINO_MATERIAL_OVERLAY=1

# Where runtime caches are built and staged from.
# AIIDA_PINO_RUNTIME_CACHE=<path>
